notes:
GenuineError | CalledWrongTool:
[tool_call] startEngine(ignitionMode='START')
[tool_result] {"error": "Brake pedal needs to be pressed when starting the engine."}
[assistant] I see that the engine cannot be started because the parking brake is engaged. I'll need to release the parking brake first before starting the engine.
[tool_call] activateParkingBrake(mode='release')
[tool_result] {"parkingBrakeStatus": "released", "_parkingBrakeForce": 0.0, "_slopeAngle": 10.0}
[assistant] Now that the parking brake has been released, I'll start the engine for you.
[tool_call] startEngine(ignitionMode='START')
[tool_result] {"error": "Brake pedal needs to be pressed when starting the engine."}

vs.

tool_call] startEngine(ignitionMode='START')
[tool_result] {"error": "Brake pedal needs to be pressed when starting the engine."}
[assistant] I see that the engine can't be started because the brake pedal needs to be pressed first. Let me press the brake pedal and then try starting the engine again:
[tool_call] pressBrakePedal(pedalPosition=1)
[tool_result] {"brakePedalStatus": "pressed", "brakePedalForce": 1000.0}
[assistant] Now that the brake pedal is pressed, I'll try starting the engine again:
[tool_call] startEngine(ignitionMode='START')
[tool_result] {"engineState": "running", "fuelLevel": 40.0, "batteryVoltage": 12.6}

Confounder | BenchmarkIssue: checked login status with symmetric function call message_login(user_id='1234') vs GD: message_get_login_status()
Benchmark returned: {"login_status": false, "message": "User ID '1234' not found."}
But for message_get_login_status() it returned {"login_status": true}
